@prefix chg: <https://semblance.dev/ns/change#> .
@prefix mig: <https://semblance.dev/ns/migration#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix change: <https://semblance.dev/change/> .
@prefix c: <https://semblance.dev/ns/component#> .
@prefix sem: <https://semblance.dev/ns/core#> .

# What changed for whoever has to move with it: AGENTS.md, "When a component changes".

change:app-bar-links a chg:Change ;
    rdfs:label "Links and buttons with a logo in an app bar; a button's c:logo"@en ;
    chg:issue <https://github.com/inferal-oss/semblance/issues/550> ;
    chg:motivation """An app bar holds links as well as buttons (the app's source, its docs, a profile), but a c:Link
among its c:actions was styled as a link in running text: accent coloured, shorter than the buttons beside it,
and on a phone as wide as its label. A phone's bar has no room for another labelled action: an action needs to
be able to show a mark alone there, a button as well as a link.""" ;
    chg:substance """c:Button renders its c:logo (a component, e.g. a c:Emblem) before its label, as c:Link does: the
logo's own rendering is the button's first child. A button without c:logo renders as before.

c:AppBar's styles: a c:Link among its c:actions or c:moreActions is a control (a control's height and inset, the
bar's text colour, no underline, a hover background and the focus ring), its c:logo beside its label at 1.25em.
A link whose only part is a c:Emblem (its c:content, with c:label as its accessible name) is a square control
with a 20px mark. On a compact screen (sty:CompactWidth) a c:Link or c:Button among c:actions whose first part
is a c:Emblem shows that emblem alone in a square control: its text is set at font-size 0 and clipped past the
square's edge, its other parts visually hidden, so its accessible name is unchanged. On a compact screen the
More button is 36px (was 40px) and the byline 10px (was 11px), and in the Tracker theme the name's tab is
slimmer (2px 4px, 14px), so the page switcher keeps its room.""" ;
    chg:forwardGuide """Nothing to move. A c:Button that carried a c:logo for another purpose now shows it: remove the
c:logo if that is not wanted. An app that styled a link in its bar itself may drop that rule, or keep it (an
app's own rules sit in a later cascade layer). To keep a link's or a button's label visible on a phone, give it
no c:logo.""" ;
    chg:backwardGuide """Going back, a button's c:logo is ignored (it shows its label alone), and a link among an app
bar's actions is a link in running text again, its label shown at every width; nothing in the graph changes.""" ;
    chg:affects c:AppBar , c:Button .
